## Permission matrix

<!-- table:personas.permissions role=register id=Role -->

| Role | Read | Create | Modify | Approve | Close |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|

Rules, inherited from the reference architecture and non-negotiable:

- **Role comes from the authenticated session only** — never from client input, a header, or a request body.
- **Reads default to authenticated staff; writes are allow-listed per role.**
- **Every write names an approver role.** Nothing writes because it seemed reasonable at runtime.
- At least one role should be read-only, and it should be the one that audits.

## Write allow-list

The complete set of things an agent may change. Enumerated here, derived from approved use cases.

<!-- table:personas.write-allow-list role=register id=Id -->

| Id | Write | Object | Roles permitted | Approver | Reversible | Use case |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

`WR-NN`, minted at accept time like every other id. It is the join key: the
ontology compiler names every generated write template `wr-NN-<slug>` in every
target, so a write that changes its id changes a filename two repos away.

